  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDEHA - interoperability data ecosystems for humanitarian assistance, global action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Effective humanitarian response requires collaboration and information sharing across various partners and technical sectors to provide timely assistance, save lives, and enhance living conditions. Having multiple access points through sectoral assistance to reach vulnerable populations may be considered as efficient and rapid service delivery. However, conducting numerous registrations and household needs assessments can lead to inclusion or exclusion errors, delays in aid delivery, inadequate targeting, and survey fatigue among affected individuals. The proposed action is about consolidating the best practices in South Sudan, Somalia and fostering a collaborative approach. IOM aims to extend these practices to interested organizations and consortia, inviting them to join us in this critical endeavour and replicate them in other countries. Therefore, under the proposed action, IOM aims to contribute to a collaborative ecosystem for optimizing a coordinated approach for greater impact in the global integrated humanitarian response.</narrative>
  </description>
